1639
01:10:11.600 --> 01:10:13.680
Oh, yes, there was.

1640
01:10:13.940 --> 01:10:15.900
There was a very big scene.

1641
01:10:16.080 --> 01:10:16.680
It was deleted.

1642
01:10:16.900 --> 01:10:21.980
It would have come after the next scene when Pam and Andy go into Daryl's office.

1643
01:10:21.980 --> 01:10:25.020
Yes, so Daryl is bummed about Val's boyfriend.

1644
01:10:25.240 --> 01:10:25.520
Uh-huh.

1645
01:10:25.940 --> 01:10:27.280
Andy and Pam go into his office.

1646
01:10:27.460 --> 01:10:28.860
Andy's saying, play it cool.

1647
01:10:29.060 --> 01:10:29.980
Val will come around.

1648
01:10:30.160 --> 01:10:32.200
And Pam says, no, just go for it.

1649
01:10:32.320 --> 01:10:36.100
And Andy says, no, Jim would tell you to play it cool.

1650
01:10:36.280 --> 01:10:39.680
And Pam says, Jim would tell you to go for it.

1651
01:10:39.840 --> 01:10:40.020
Yeah.

1652
01:10:40.180 --> 01:10:42.660
So now the scene would have extended.

1653
01:10:42.980 --> 01:10:44.440
It's in deleted scenes.

1654
01:10:44.440 --> 01:10:45.540
It would have continued.

1655
01:10:45.540 --> 01:10:47.800
And Pam would have said, well, you know what?

1656
01:10:48.060 --> 01:10:49.660
Let's call Jim and ask him.

1657
01:10:49.660 --> 01:10:52.800
Basically, she's debating with Andy.

1658
01:10:53.060 --> 01:10:54.180
Is Andy right?

1659
01:10:54.320 --> 01:10:55.660
Is Jim going to say play it cool?

1660
01:10:55.800 --> 01:10:56.780
Or am I right?

1661
01:10:56.780 --> 01:10:57.580
I'm his wife.

1662
01:10:57.780 --> 01:10:58.120
Yes.

1663
01:10:58.220 --> 01:10:59.160
I think I know my husband.

1664
01:10:59.420 --> 01:11:06.000
So somehow by memory, she knows Jim's hotel room number in Tallahassee.

1665
01:11:06.160 --> 01:11:07.780
And she puts this on speakerphone.

1666
01:11:08.220 --> 01:11:10.220
And Kathy answers the phone.

1667
01:11:10.620 --> 01:11:10.920
Yeah.

1668
01:11:11.380 --> 01:11:15.320
And Andy and Daryl and Pam are all like, huh.

1669
01:11:15.560 --> 01:11:16.760
So let's hear it.

1670
01:11:18.480 --> 01:11:19.960
Let's call Jim.

1671
01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:23.880
You're going to be embarrassed.

1672
01:11:24.100 --> 01:11:24.680
You think so?

1673
01:11:25.720 --> 01:11:26.200
Okay.

1674
01:11:26.640 --> 01:11:27.320
We'll see.

1675
01:11:27.860 --> 01:11:28.220
He'll tell you.

1676
01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:30.900
Uh, hello?

1677
01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:31.600
Who is this?

1678
01:11:37.860 --> 01:11:38.340
Hello.

1679
01:11:41.600 --> 01:11:42.080
Yeah.

1680
01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:44.660
Yeah, I'm here with Andy and Daryl.

1681
01:11:44.900 --> 01:11:45.220
Do not.

1682
01:11:45.380 --> 01:11:46.680
What are you and Kathy up to?

1683
01:11:47.140 --> 01:11:48.040
Watching a game.

1684
01:11:48.280 --> 01:11:49.120
Do you guys alone?

1685
01:11:49.460 --> 01:11:51.100
Or did everyone come up from the bar?

1686
01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:52.380
Just me and Kathy now.

1687
01:11:58.580 --> 01:11:59.380
Don't do it.

1688
01:12:00.080 --> 01:12:01.020
Or do do it.

1689
01:12:01.340 --> 01:12:02.140
Whatever it is.

1690
01:12:02.240 --> 01:12:02.900
This is awesome.

1691
01:12:03.640 --> 01:12:05.540
Uh, hey, babe, is Einstein with you?

1692
01:12:06.020 --> 01:12:06.420
No.

1693
01:12:09.350 --> 01:12:12.570
Einstein is the codename we use if we're ever caught in a home invasion scenario.

1694
01:12:14.510 --> 01:12:15.970
As a parent, you think of these things.

1695
01:12:17.530 --> 01:12:19.550
Okay, so there's a lot of things happening here.

1696
01:12:19.750 --> 01:12:20.710
A lot of things to unpack.

1697
01:12:21.230 --> 01:12:22.450
Pam is weirded out.

1698
01:12:22.870 --> 01:12:24.250
And like Kelly comes in.

1699
01:12:24.390 --> 01:12:25.890
Kelly's having the best night of her life.

1700
01:12:25.990 --> 01:12:26.950
So much gossip.

1701
01:12:26.950 --> 01:12:28.670
Yes, so much is happening.

1702
01:12:28.850 --> 01:12:30.530
It's the best night of her life, basically.

1703
01:12:31.070 --> 01:12:35.390
Okay, so this kind of started something that never got resolved.

1704
01:12:35.630 --> 01:12:37.970
This was my complaint that I was talking about earlier,

1705
01:12:38.270 --> 01:12:41.610
which is that you were going to see Pam get insecure,

1706
01:12:41.610 --> 01:12:47.150
and you were also going to see everyone in the office assume something was going on between Jim and Kathy.

1707
01:12:47.370 --> 01:12:47.630
Yeah, yeah.

1708
01:12:47.930 --> 01:12:48.750
Kelly's so excited.

1709
01:12:49.070 --> 01:12:52.410
And so because of that, John and I were like,

1710
01:12:52.510 --> 01:12:56.210
you have to write a scene that resolves this insecurity in Pam.

1711
01:12:56.210 --> 01:12:57.210
Pam, you have to.

1712
01:12:57.850 --> 01:12:58.830
So they did.

1713
01:12:58.830 --> 01:13:02.630
And then there was another scene that we shot that was also deleted.

1714
01:13:03.170 --> 01:13:04.550
Jim and Pam are on the phone.

1715
01:13:04.730 --> 01:13:05.810
It would have played a little later.

1716
01:13:06.250 --> 01:13:07.150
Should we listen to that one?

1717
01:13:07.250 --> 01:13:07.490
Yeah.

1718
01:13:08.470 --> 01:13:10.030
She's still sitting right there.

1719
01:13:10.210 --> 01:13:11.810
You know she's lying about the heating.

1720
01:13:12.250 --> 01:13:13.070
Of course.

1721
01:13:13.570 --> 01:13:14.590
I feel bad for her.

1722
01:13:14.890 --> 01:13:15.990
It's really pathetic.

1723
01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:18.330
Yes, it is.

1724
01:13:19.150 --> 01:13:20.850
I wish I was there to see your face.

1725
01:13:21.130 --> 01:13:23.110
You always look really cute when you're embarrassed.

1726
01:13:23.950 --> 01:13:24.390
Okay.

1727
01:13:24.810 --> 01:13:25.570
Ha, ha, ha.

1728
01:13:26.070 --> 01:13:26.790
I love you.

1729
01:13:26.890 --> 01:13:27.570
I'll talk to you later.

1730
01:13:27.690 --> 01:13:28.410
Have fun with that.

1731
01:13:29.150 --> 01:13:29.990
Love you too.

1732
01:13:30.450 --> 01:13:31.450
I will not.

1733
01:13:35.420 --> 01:13:36.680
Nice to hear her voice.

1734
01:13:37.580 --> 01:13:39.420
Scranton building three miles away, right?

1735
01:13:41.160 --> 01:13:46.960
So the point of that one was to show that like Pam is on to Kathy, she is in no way insecure.

1736
01:13:47.280 --> 01:13:47.620
Yeah.

1737
01:13:47.620 --> 01:13:50.200
And in fact is somewhat amused by Jim's predicament.

1738
01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:50.540
Yeah.

1739
01:13:50.700 --> 01:13:51.700
She's like, enjoy that.

1740
01:13:51.780 --> 01:13:52.980
He's like, I will not.

1741
01:13:53.720 --> 01:13:58.920
Well, you know, Warren said if you watch the deleted scene, you can tell it doesn't play

1742
01:13:58.920 --> 01:14:01.620
because the audience gets both halves.

1743
01:14:01.820 --> 01:14:06.180
They get on the front end, Pam in the office trying to mask her anxiety about it.

1744
01:14:06.180 --> 01:14:12.340
But then on the B side, you can hear her do a complete 180 and she's totally at ease.

1745
01:14:12.520 --> 01:14:15.660
And when they watch them, it just didn't match.

1746
01:14:15.660 --> 01:14:16.480
And it was cut.

1747
01:14:16.780 --> 01:14:17.740
No, I agree.

1748
01:14:17.740 --> 01:14:18.920
It didn't really play.

1749
01:14:19.540 --> 01:14:24.160
But by cutting it out, it kind of ends with the audience knowing that Jim ultimately spent

1750
01:14:24.160 --> 01:14:24.940
the night with Dwight.

1751
01:14:25.100 --> 01:14:27.880
But we don't know if Jim ever told Pam about this.

1752
01:14:28.020 --> 01:14:31.980
And you have to remember, both Stanley and Dwight know that Kathy was in Jim's room.

1753
01:14:31.980 --> 01:14:35.540
I mean, someone's going to end up saying something back at the office.

1754
01:14:35.660 --> 01:14:40.900
Like, even if this phone call never happened, people still know Kathy was in Jim's room.

1755
01:14:41.060 --> 01:14:43.120
You know Stanley's going to tell Phyllis.

1756
01:14:43.280 --> 01:14:44.140
A hundred percent.

1757
01:14:44.140 --> 01:14:46.680
And then Phyllis is going to tell somebody.

1758
01:14:47.100 --> 01:14:48.300
Well, here's what happened.

1759
01:14:48.440 --> 01:14:52.720
I told you I was at the hotel because I was going to do the other side of my phone call dialogue.

1760
01:14:52.920 --> 01:14:53.100
Right.

1761
01:14:53.320 --> 01:14:56.240
Well, I was just watching all of this play out.

1762
01:14:56.420 --> 01:15:00.180
Like, all of like the way Jim was playing it, the way Kathy was playing it.

1763
01:15:00.180 --> 01:15:03.000
And John and I were so in our heads about this.

1764
01:15:03.100 --> 01:15:08.500
We just were so nervous about how Jim was going to come across and how the relationship

1765
01:15:08.500 --> 01:15:09.520
was going to come across.

1766
01:15:09.860 --> 01:15:13.640
And we had one of those moments that had not happened in a very long time.

1767
01:15:14.040 --> 01:15:14.480
I know.

1768
01:15:14.700 --> 01:15:19.040
It became, I mean, these moments when they did happen, it was like screech.

1769
01:15:19.260 --> 01:15:20.680
Like, all filming stopped.

1770
01:15:20.920 --> 01:15:21.140
Yeah.

1771
01:15:21.300 --> 01:15:22.660
They kind of shut down the set.

1772
01:15:22.760 --> 01:15:27.820
And we had this huge discussion with Warren and Halstead and Brian.

1773
01:15:28.060 --> 01:15:28.940
Paul got in on it.

